# The toolbox, one program per line. `just link` builds tools/ from this file
# and case 18 of the suite fails if the directory and this list disagree.
#
# `ply -t tools` makes PATH this directory alone, so the model reaches these
# and cannot name one that is not here. It **aims** the model; it does not
# sandbox it -- sh has builtins and a redirect opens a file with no program
# involved. The boundary is the container, which is why the builder runs in
# one. Saying otherwise would be the lie ply's SECURITY.md exists to prevent.

# read
ls
cat
head
tail
grep
find
diff
wc

# write
sed
awk
mkdir
mv
cp
rm
touch

# the check, and the runtime it needs. page-check's shebang is
# `/usr/bin/env node`, and with PATH set to this directory alone that lookup
# happens *here* -- so a toolbox without node is a checker the model cannot
# run itself, and it would then be blind between cycles.
node
page-check
